WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.502
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.904
to the captain's quarters
on the S.S. Pandemic.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.140
As we've established, I found
my way here via a portal

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.744
that connects my attic door
to my in-laws' fireplace,

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.177
leading many of you to ask,

00:00:12.177 --> 00:00:14.847
"What's happening in the attic
now that you're gone?"

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.650
Well, according to my dear
friend and attic sitter,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.652
Ethan Hawke, the wasps

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.487
have taken over
the cameras and are filming

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.356
their very own late night show.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.358
But apparently they spend
the whole time complaining

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.460
about this one moth who's
king of the insects.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.161
And, I don't know,
to me it sounds like

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:30.830
that would get pretty
repetitive.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.665
And speaking of dumb jokes,

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.801
the president shook up
his flailing campaign

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.804
as the coronavirus outbreak
spirals further out of control.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.973
And now, he's honing in on two
key reelection strategies --

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.643
less testing and more racism.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.912
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.449
♪♪

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.417
Given that the country is
currently on fire

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.919
after a once-in-a-century
cataclysm inflamed

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.721
by the president's cruelty
and incompetence,

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.090
he's had some trouble

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.458
coming up with a solid
re-election message.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.094
It's not a great sign when your
own campaign manager

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:05.732
is advertising face masks
with your name on them.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.867
Each breath you take could be
the one that kills you!

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.502
Four more years?

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.372
Which is why he called a fake
press conference on Tuesday

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.507
to spin his wheels
and try out yet another

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.109
deranged campaign message --

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:19.011
the Democrats want to
abolish everything.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:20.647
-These are actual key elements

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:24.150
of the Biden-Sanders
unity platform.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.052
Abolish immigration detention.

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:30.423
They're going to abolish
immigration enforcement.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.127
Abolish law enforcement
as we know it.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:37.263
Abolish completely
the death penalty.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.033
They want to abolish
our police departments.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.235
They want to abolish
our prisons, I guess.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:46.105
Abolish all charter schools.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:49.041
Abolish
educational standards.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:51.677
Abolish in the suburbs --

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:53.613
You're going to abolish
the suburbs with this.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.782
-First of all, most of that
sounds awesome.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.917
All you're doing is listing
a bunch of things people hate

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.652
and claiming the Democrats
will get rid of them.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:02.488
"Democrats want to abolish
telemarketers, the DMV,

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.623
gate-crashing at the airport,
and in-laws."

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.159
And of course, I would never
abolish in-laws.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.096
If someone else owned this
house, they'd probably want me

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.531
to cease taping a television
show immediately.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.800
Also, I love
how transparent he is

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.003
that he's just making stuff up
when he says,

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.671
"They want to abolish prisons,
I guess."

00:02:19.671 --> 00:02:21.841
He sounds like your dad
describing a movie he saw on TNT

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.409
last night as he was
falling asleep.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.710
"They were on a boat, I guess,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.712
and Tom Hanks was in it,
I think.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:29.815
It was just a disagreement
as to who was captain."

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:31.450
-I'm the captain.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.086
-Oh, sorry, I wasn't
talking about you.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.753
-Okay.

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:36.789
-Third, when Trump said
Democrats want to abolish

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.724
the suburbs, he was talking
about a program

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:41.694
implemented by the Obama
administration to desegregate

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:45.364
the suburbs by enforcing
the Fair Housing Act of 1968,

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:46.932
which outlawed
discrimination

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:48.634
and racial segregation
in housing.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.604
So not only was Trump's lie
racist, it was absurd.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.640
He makes it sound like Democrats
are trying to ban

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.341
strip malls and cul-de-sacs.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.943
"They want to take away
your Hot Topics

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.411
and your Auntie Anne's.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.379
But we're not gonna let that
happen, folks."

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:02.815
Without suburbs, who will
borrow our pruning shears

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.183
and not return them?

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.051
Where will our adorable
space aliens land

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.286
and befriend our children?

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:10.222
Where will our fathers
painstakingly restore

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.057
classic cars in a vein
and desperate attempt

00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:13.793
to recapture their youth?

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:17.129
This is all Trump has left,
racist grievance politics.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.465
In the middle
of a raging pandemic

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.234
that is spiraling out
of control,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.302
has killed nearly
140,000 Americans,

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.705
and put tens of millions
out of work, the president

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.007
took time out of his day to pose

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.075
with a bunch of Goya
food products

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:32.044
on the Oval Office desk.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:35.080
Well, at least he didn't have to
clear anything off his desk

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.783
to take this photo.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.951
He looks like a divorcée
trying to prove he's fine

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:42.154
by posting on Facebook,
"About to make dinner.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:45.091
So sorry, Leslie, I guess I can
do this by myself."

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.293
But at least that smile --
that smile

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.262
on the president's face
is sincere.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.230
Let's punch in on that.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.898
Jesus.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.034
He looks like he just took
a big swig of ice water

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.303
and forgot he had
a temporary filling.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.772
The U.S. set a record for new
daily coronavirus cases

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.174
on Tuesday,
but by all means,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.208
celebrate with
a chocolate wafer.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:06.278
And to anyone who would promote
a product from the Oval Office

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:09.515
during a pandemic,
Goya [bleep] yourself.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.750
-Good one, Seth.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.319
-Thank you, Captain.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:16.288
-Thank you for the wordplay.

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:18.490
-The thing is, none of this
is working.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.594
Yesterday, Trump got yet another
devastating poll result

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.030
when Quinnipiac found
that he was behind by Biden

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.333
by 15 points, and that a
stunning 60 percent of Americans

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.535
disapprove of Trump's
job performance.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.504
I guess my only question about
that is, who are the other 40?

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.774
Do they all work
at the Lysol factory?

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.909
And yes, I know we've been
here before,

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.744
so we absolutely must be
cautious.

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.046
It is by no means a given
that Trump will lose.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:43.383
But as NBC News reported
this week, the Trump campaign

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:46.185
has struggled to land
a punch on Biden.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.521
As NBC reported, the Trump
campaign feels like

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.990
none of the president's
attacks have worked.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.626
He has tried tagging Biden as
untrustworthy -- "Corrupt Joe"

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.294
and lethargic --
"Sleepy Joe" --

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:58.497
but it hasn't dragged Biden down
with voters as Trump had hoped.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:00.566
"Sleepy sounds pretty good
when you've had four years

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.636
of exhaustion," a White House
official quipped.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.939
And it's hard to tag someone
else as sleepy and corrupt

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.408
when you look
like a Mafia don

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:11.043
who falls asleep
in his spaghetti.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:14.546
But yeah, "Sleepy" sounds
great, and that's Biden.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.148
He's a human Ambien.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.050
He's so boring that even when
he starts telling a story

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.619
about some knife fight
between rival gangs

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:22.822
at a public pool, your
first reaction is to say,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.723
"Don't start until
I get my blanket!"

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:26.225
And that's great.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.427
You know what I'd give to go
one day without waking up

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.296
and immediately seeing
six different news alerts

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.431
on my phone about crazy [bleep]
the president did?

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:35.300
At this point, I'd vote for one
of those drinking birds.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.336
So now Trump is shaking up
his campaign,

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.372
demoting his campaign manager,
Brad Parscale,

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:42.307
after the campaign's
embarrassing Tulsa debacle,

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:44.610
in which Trump spoke to
an empty arena that somehow

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.313
also managed to seed
a coronavirus outbreak.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:50.282
And I'm no expert,
but generally speaking,

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:52.718
things are not going great
when you're firing

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:55.455
your campaign manager 100 days
before the election.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:58.424
That's like a jockey jumping off
his horse in the home stretch

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.826
and deciding to run
the rest of the way.

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.562
But hey, at least Parscale can
go back to his old job

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.297
as the, I don't know,

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:08.734
drummer for a Norwegian
black metal band?

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:11.137
Dude looks like an out-of-shape
Conor McGregor.

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.906
Trump's campaign is sputtering
because the coronavirus crisis

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.508
isn't a problem Trump can
just B.S. his away out of.

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:19.378
It's a real thing with
real consequences,

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.214
and the only way to make those
go away is by governing,

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:24.150
which is just not
in his skill set.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.351
In fact, when it comes to
actually governing,

00:06:26.351 --> 00:06:28.487
Trump has had one very
specific obsession

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.856
since the start of the this
pandemic, and that's

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:34.326
his obsession with slowing down
testing for coronavirus

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:37.062
so he can hide the numbers and
make himself him look better.

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:40.966
And because Trump isn't just a
criminal, but a dumb criminal,

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:43.202
he has openly confessed
to this many times.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.737
One of the first times
was in back in March

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.605
when he said publicly
that he would prefer

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:50.476
not to let American coronavirus
patients off a cruise ship,

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.611
because it would make
the numbers worse.

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:56.148 line:0%
-I mean, frankly,
if it were up to me,

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:59.218 line:0%
I would be inclined to say,
"Leave everybody on the ship

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.388 line:0%
for a period of time and
use the ship as your base."

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:05.457 line:0%
But a lot of people would rather
do it a different way.

00:07:05.457 --> 00:07:07.459 line:0%
They would rather quarantine
people when they land.

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:10.329 line:0%
Now, when they do that, our
numbers are going to go up,

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.997 line:0%
Okay?
Our numbers are going to go up.

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:13.699 line:0%
They would like to have
the people come off.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.767 line:0%
I'd like to have the people
stay, but I'd go with them.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.603 line:0%
I told them to make
the final decision.

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:19.871 line:0%
I would rather --
because I like the numbers

00:07:19.871 --> 00:07:21.707 line:0%
being where they are.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:25.878 line:0%
I don't need to have the numbers
double because of one ship.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:28.847 line:0%
I'd rather have them stay on,
personally.

00:07:28.847 --> 00:07:30.650
-That's right.
President Jigsaw over here

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.051
openly said he wanted to keep
Americans trapped on an infected

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:36.321
cruise ship like some sort of
coronavirus-themed escape room.

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:38.190
Which, even if there was
no coronavirus

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.359
would still be a punishment,
because no one ever leaves

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.595
an escape room happier
than when they entered.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.431
In my experience, there's always
a fight or whose fault it was

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:47.033
that you couldn't solve
the riddle hidden under

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:49.001
the fortuneteller's
crystal ball or whatever.

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.103
"Beth, I told you there was
a clue in the tarot cards,

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:53.906
but you spent all your time
rubbing the magic genie lamp!

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:56.575
Happy birthday, Beth,
and go to hell!"

00:07:56.575 --> 00:07:58.644
Trump has repeated this desire
to hide the true extent

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.379
of the crisis from Americans
many times.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.448
At a White House event
on Monday, for example,

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:05.617
a reporter asked him about
the lie that more testing

00:08:05.617 --> 00:08:07.753
leads to more cases,
and he offered this

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:10.289
truly incoherent response.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.792 line:0%
-President Trump, you've said
many times that the number

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:16.929 line:0%
of coronavirus cases is going up
because testing is increasing.

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.431 line:0%
-That's right.
-Do you acknowledge

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:20.866 line:0%
that it's going up
for other reasons, too?

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.269 line:0%
For example, that it's actually
spreading?

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:26.172 line:0%
And what are you going to do
to stop the spread?

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:27.973
-Well, you know that we have
one of the lowest

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:30.409
mortality rates anywhere.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:33.578
If you know, Biden and Obama
stopped their testing.

00:08:33.578 --> 00:08:35.548
They just stopped it.
You probably know that.

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.182
I'm sure you don't want to
report it.

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:39.885
But they stopped testing.

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:42.855
Right in the middle, they just
went, "No more testing,"

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:47.226
and on a much lesser problem
than the problem that we have,

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:49.295
obviously, with respect to

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:53.432
this is the worst thing that's
happened since probably 1917.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.100
This is a very bad --
all over the world.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.503
It's 188 countries right now.

00:08:57.503 --> 00:09:00.673
But, no, we are -- we test more
than anybody, by far.

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:02.908
And when you test,
you create cases.

00:09:02.908 --> 00:09:04.477
So we've created cases.

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:06.745
-Okay. There's so much
brain diarrhea

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:08.514
to wade through here,
I might have to borrow

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:10.016
the sea captain's ship.

00:09:10.016 --> 00:09:12.351
-Arrgh, she's hearty vessel!

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:15.387
But no match for that
rusty chop!

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:16.955
-Gross, okay.

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:18.991
First of all, you're not
"creating" cases.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.727
The cases are there, whether you
test for them or not.

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.963
You don't "create" a fire
by putting a smoke alarm

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:25.530
in your house.
If someone gets sick,

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:27.733
they're sick whether they
get tested or not.

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.168
It's not like they're at home
lying in bed with

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:31.770
a 104-degree fever
and no sense of taste or smell

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.705
saying, hey, "As long
as I don't get tested,

00:09:33.705 --> 00:09:35.274
I don't have
to get treated!

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:39.378
Now to spend the next three days
crawling to my kitchen."

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.447
Second, why do you keep saying

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:45.184
the 1918 Spanish flu pandemic
happened in 1917?

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:47.052
Trump has said this more times
than I can count,

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:50.088
and apparently just no one
has corrected him.

00:09:50.088 --> 00:09:53.592
-We have a very unusual
situation

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.794
where something came
in that nobody has seen

00:09:55.794 --> 00:09:57.797
for many, many decades,

00:09:57.797 --> 00:10:00.799
probably 1917 would be
the closest analogy,

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:02.034
if you look at it.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.535
The likes of which this world

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:06.739
has not seen since 1917.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:09.708
Nothing like this since 1917.

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:13.779
Last time was -- of this
magnitude, 1917.

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.313
That's a long time ago.

00:10:15.313 --> 00:10:18.918
-We haven't seen anything like
this in 100 and some-odd years.

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:20.485
1917.

00:10:20.485 --> 00:10:23.922
But 1917, so that's over
100 years ago.

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:27.526
1917, which was the greatest
of them all.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.227
Right? 1917.

00:10:29.227 --> 00:10:32.698
